  <ferc:NameOfOfficerWithCustodyOfCorporateBooks id="f-1" contextRef="c-1">Kimberly Stinson</ferc:NameOfOfficerWithCustodyOfCorporateBooks>
  <ferc:TitleOfOfficerWithCustodyOfCorporateBooks id="f-2" contextRef="c-1">Corporate Controller, EQT Corporation</ferc:TitleOfOfficerWithCustodyOfCorporateBooks>
  <ferc:AddressWhereCorporateBooksAreKept id="f-3" contextRef="c-1">2200 Energy Drive, Canonsburg, PA 15317</ferc:AddressWhereCorporateBooksAreKept>
  <ferc:IncorporationDate id="f-4" contextRef="c-1">2014-08-22</ferc:IncorporationDate>
  <ferc:GeneralInformationAboutStatesInWhichRespondentServicesWereRendered id="f-5" contextRef="c-1">Mountain Valley Pipeline, LLC is a natural gas company under the Natural Gas Act and is engaged in the transmission of natural gas in West Virginia and Virginia.</ferc:GeneralInformationAboutStatesInWhichRespondentServicesWereRendered>
  <ferc:GeneralInformationChangeInAuditorFlag id="f-6" contextRef="c-1">false</ferc:GeneralInformationChangeInAuditorFlag>
  <ferc:StateOfIncorporation id="f-7" contextRef="c-1">DE</ferc:StateOfIncorporation>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInAndImportantAdditionsToFranchiseRightsTextBlock id="f-8" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;1. None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInAndImportantAdditionsToFranchiseRightsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfAcquisitionOfOwnershipInOtherCompaniesByReorganizationMergerOrConsolidationWithOtherCompaniesTextBlock id="f-9" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2. None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfAcquisitionOfOwnershipInOtherCompaniesByReorganizationMergerOrConsolidationWithOtherCompaniesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock id="f-10" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;3. None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock id="f-11" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;4. None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock id="f-12" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;5. None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="f-13" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;6. None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock id="f-14" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;7. Mountain Valley Pipeline, LLC (the Company) is organized under the Third Amended and Restated Limited Liability Company Agreement, dated April 6, 2018, as amended by that certain First Amendment, dated February 5, 2020, and that certain Second Amendment, dated November 1, 2025 (as amended, the MVP LLC Agreement).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Effective November 1, 2025, the MVP LLC Agreement was amended to provide for, among other things, the formation of Mountain Valley Pipeline, LLC &#8211; Series C (MVP C), a series of the Company. The amendment establishes the governance and organizational provisions for MVP C.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock id="f-15" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;8. None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock id="f-16" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;9. None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock id="f-17" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;10. None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedIncreaseOrDecreaseInAnnualRevenuesCausedByImportantRateChangesTextBlock id="f-18" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;11. None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedIncreaseOrDecreaseInAnnualRevenuesCausedByImportantRateChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock id="f-19" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;12. The Company does not have officers. EQM Gathering Opco, LLC (EQM Gathering), the Company's operator, has officers responsible for the operation of the Company's systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On May 30, 2025, Robert R. Wingo provided notice of his decision to resign from his role as President and Manager of EQM Gathering, effective June 20, 2025. Effective December 31, 2025, Toby Z. Rice was appointed Manager and President of EQM Gathering. In addition, effective December 31, 2025, the following changes were made: (i) J.E.B. Bolen was appointed as Manager and Vice President of EQM Gathering; (ii) Michael Ender and Charity Fleenor were appointed as Vice Presidents of EQM Gathering; and (iii) Michael Lauderbaugh was removed from his role as Vice President of EQM Gathering.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Each series of the Company has a Management Committee.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Effective June 20, 2025, Mr. Wingo resigned from the Management Committees of Mountain Valley Pipeline, LLC &#8211; Series A (MVP A) and Mountain Valley Pipeline, LLC &#8211; Series B (MVP B), and Jeremy Knop was appointed to succeed Mr. Wingo as the Representative of PipeBox LLC on the MVP A Management Committee and as the Representative of MVP Holdco B, LLC (previously MVP Holdco, LLC) on the MVP B Management Committee. Effective December 16, 2025, MVP Holdco, LLC transferred its interests in MVP B to MVP Holdco B LLC. Albert Girgis holds the position of "Alternate Representative" on both Management Committees.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;Effective November 1, 2025, in connection with the formation of MVP C, a Management Committee for MVP C was established and Jeremy Knop was appointed as the Representative of MVP Holdco, LLC, and Matthew Schafer was appointed as the Representative of US Marcellus Gas Infrastructure, LLC. Albert Girgis holds the position of "Alternate Representative" for MVP Holdco, LLC, and Kyle Martin holds the position of "Alternate Representative" for US Marcellus Gas Infrastructure, LLC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;The members of each series of the Company as of December 31, 2025 are disclosed in Footnote 1 on Page 122.1 of this report.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock id="f-20" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;13. None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-21" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;A. Description of Business&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Nature of Business. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Mountain Valley Pipeline, LLC (the Company) is a Delaware series limited liability company formed as a joint venture for the purpose of constructing and owning natural gas assets. The Company has three series, as follows: MVP A, which owns MVP Mainline; MVP B, which owns the MVP Southgate project; and MVP C, which owns certain assets associated with the MVP Boost project (each term defined and described below).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;MVP LLC Agreement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company is organized under the Mountain Valley Pipeline, LLC's Third Amended and Restated Limited Liability Company Agreement, dated April 6, 2018, as amended by that certain First Amendment, dated February 5, 2020, and that certain Second Amendment, dated November 1, 2025 (as amended, the MVP LLC Agreement)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;COM Agreements. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;MVP A and MVP C are parties to that certain Second Amended and Restated Construction, Operations and Management Agreement with EQM Gathering Opco, LLC (EQM Gathering), a wholly owned subsidiary of EQT Corporation (EQT), dated November 1, 2025 (the Series A and C COM Agreement). The Series A and C COM Agreement replaced that certain Amended and Restated Construction, Operation and Management Agreement, by and between MVP A and EQM Gathering, dated June 16, 2015.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;MVP B is party to that certain Construction, Operation and Management Agreement with EQM Gathering, dated April 6, 2018, as amended by that certain First Amended thereto dated October 3, 2025 (the Series B COM Agreement and, together with the Series A and C COM Agreement, the COM Agreements).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Under the COM Agreements, EQM Gathering serves as operator of the Company and is responsible for construction, operation and management services with respect to MVP A, MVP B and MVP C. EQT's employees provide operational support and manage the Company's daily business operations. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On July 22, 2024, EQT completed its acquisition of Equitrans Midstream Corporation (Equitrans Midstream and, such acquisition, the Equitrans Midstream Merger). Prior to the Equitrans Midstream Merger, EQM Gathering was a subsidiary of Equitrans Midstream, and operational support for the Company was provided by Equitrans Midstream.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Mountain Valley Pipeline, LLC &#8211; Series A (MVP A).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;MVP A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;is a series of the Company that was formed for the purpose of constructing and owning the Mountain Valley Pipeline (MVP Mainline) and related facilities. MVP Mainline is a 303-mile long, 42-inch diameter natural gas interstate pipeline with a total capacity of 2.0 billion cubic feet (Bcf) per day that spans from Wetzel County, West Virginia to Pittsylvania County, Virginia.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;MVP Mainline entered into service on June 14, 2024 and commenced long-term firm capacity obligations on July 1, 2024. MVP Mainline is fully subscribed at a total of 2.0 Bcf per day of firm capacity commitments at 20-year terms.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company has applied for regulatory approval for a compression expansion project intended to increase capacity on the MVP Mainline. See discussion of MVP C and MVP Boost below.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;As of December 31, 2025, MVP A's members consist of PipeBox LLC (PipeBox), a joint venture in which a wholly owned subsidiary of EQT is a member, and wholly owned subsidiaries of each of NextEra Energy, Inc. (NextEra), AltaGas Ltd. (AltaGas), Con Edison Gas Pipeline and Storage, LLC (ConEd), RGC Resources, Inc. (RGC) and VED NPI IV, LLC (Vega). As of December 31, 2025, each member&#8217;s ownership interest in MVP A was as follows: PipeBox &#8211; 49.31%; NextEra &#8211; 33.36%; AltaGas &#8211; 10.00%; ConEd &#8211; 6.60%; RGC &#8211; 0.73%; and Vega &#8211; 0.00%. Vega's interest in MVP A has limited rights and obligations relative to the other MVP A members, as set forth in the MVP LLC Agreement. See "MVP A and MVP C Buy-Out Right" below for a discussion of changes in ownership interests occurring after December 31, 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Mountain Valley Pipeline, LLC &#8211; Series B (MVP B). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;MVP B&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;is a series of the Company that was formed for the purpose of constructing and owning the MVP Southgate project (MVP Southgate) and related facilities. MVP Southgate is a contemplated interstate pipeline that was approved by the FERC. MVP Southgate was initially designed to extend approximately 75 miles from MVP Mainline in Pittsylvania County, Virginia to new delivery points in Rockingham and Alamance Counties, North Carolina using 24-inch and 16-inch diameter pipe.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;In December 2023, the Company entered into precedent agreements with Public Service Company of North Carolina, Inc. (PSNC) and Duke Energy Carolinas, LLC that contemplate an amended project and, among other things, describe certain conditions precedent to the parties' respective obligations regarding MVP Southgate. As amended, the natural gas interstate pipeline would extend approximately 31 miles from the terminus of MVP Mainline in Pittsylvania County, Virginia to planned new delivery points in Rockingham County, North Carolina using 30-inch diameter pipe and have a targeted capacity of 0.55 Bcf per day.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On February 3, 2025, the Company filed an application with the FERC seeking to amend its existing Certificate of Public Convenience and Necessity to reflect the amended project. On December 18, 2025, the FERC approved the amended Certificate. On March 23, 2026, the FERC approved the Company's request to proceed with construction of the MVP Southgate facilities in Virginia. Pending receipt of remaining regulatory approvals, MVP Southgate is expected to be placed into service by mid-2028. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;As of December 31, 2025, MVP B's members consist of wholly owned subsidiaries of each of EQT, NextEra, AltaGas and RGC. As of December 31, 2025, each member&#8217;s ownership interest in MVP B was as follows: EQT &#8211; 47.20%; NextEra &#8211; 47.20%; AltaGas &#8211; 5.10%; and RGC &#8211; 0.50%.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Mountain Valley Pipeline, LLC &#8211; Series C (MVP C). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;MVP C&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;is a series of the Company that was formed on November 1, 2025 for the purpose of constructing and owning certain assets associated with the MVP Boost project (MVP Boost). MVP Boost is a contemplated project to add compression to MVP Mainline. MVP Boost is projected to increase the capacity on MVP &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Mainline by 0.6 Bcf per day. As designed, the MVP Boost project would add compression at three existing compressor stations in West Virginia and also include the construction of a new compressor station in Montgomery County, Virginia. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On October 23, 2025, the Company applied to the FERC for authorization to construct MVP Boost. Pending receipt of regulatory approvals, MVP Boost is expected to be placed into service by mid-2028. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;As of December 31, 2025, MVP C's members consist of wholly owned subsidiaries of each of EQT, NextEra, AltaGas, ConEd, RGC and Vega. As of December 31, 2025, each member's ownership interest in MVP C was as follows: EQT &#8211; 49.31%; NextEra &#8211; 33.36%; AltaGas &#8211; 10.00%; ConEd &#8211; 6.60%; RGC &#8211; 0.73%; and Vega &#8211; 0.00%. Vega's interest in MVP C has limited rights and obligations relative to the other members, as set forth in the MVP LLC Agreement. See "MVP A and MVP C Buy-Out Right" below for a discussion of changes in ownership interests occurring after December 31, 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;MVP A and MVP C Buy-Out Rights. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On November 24, 2025, ConEd entered into a purchase and sale agreement pursuant to which ConEd agreed to sell its approximately 6.60% interest in each of MVP A and MVP C to a third-party investor. Subsequently, both PipeBox and NextEra each provided ConEd notice of their election to exercise their preferential buy-out rights in full in accordance with the MVP LLC Agreement. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On January 16, 2026, PipeBox entered into a purchase and sale agreement with ConEd to acquire ConEd's approximately 3.94% interest in MVP A and MVP C. The transaction is expected to close in the first half of 2026, subject to regulatory approvals. On January 20, 2026, NextEra completed its acquisition of ConEd's remaining approximately 2.66% interest in MVP A and MVP C.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ffffff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;----------------&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;B. Significant Accounting Policies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Basis of Presentation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;These Financial Statements were prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC as set forth in its Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP). Differences between the Financial Statements and GAAP include differences related to income taxes, purchase accounting and the classification of certain accounts in the Balance Sheets, Statements of Income and Statements of Cash Flows.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;These Financial Statements include the accounts of the Company and each of its series. As such, any intercompany accounts and transactions between the series of the Company have been eliminated. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Use of Estimates. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The preparation of financial statements in conformity with the accounting requirements of the FERC as set forth in its USofA and published accounting releases requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the amounts reported herein. Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Cash and Cash Equivalents. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company considers all highly liquid investments with an original maturity of three months or less when purchased to be cash equivalents and accounts for such investments at cost. Interest earned on cash equivalents is included in interest and dividend income. See also Note "Cash and Cash Equivalents."&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Accounts Receivable. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company's accounts receivable relate primarily to pipeline revenue. Under the Company's tariff, amounts are due within ten days of billing. Judgment is required in assessing the ultimate realization of the Company's accounts receivable. As of both December 31, 2025 and 2024, the Company recorded no provision for uncollectible accounts as all accounts receivable were current.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Fair Value Measurements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt; The carrying value of cash and cash equivalents, accounts receivable and accounts payable approximates fair value due to their short-term maturities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Properties and Depreciation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company's property, plant and equipment is stated at cost. Maintenance projects that do not increase the overall life of the related assets are expensed as incurred. Expenditures that extend the useful life of the asset are capitalized. In the ordinary course of business, the cost of property retired plus removal costs less salvage is charged to accumulated depreciation. For asset sales, the cost of property retired plus removal costs are netted against the asset's accumulated depreciation, and the residual amount is recorded as a gain or loss on disposition.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company's assets are depreciated using composite rates on a straight-line basis over the estimated useful life of the asset. The average depreciation rate for both years ended &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;December 31, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2025 and 2024 was approximately 2.5%. Depreciation rates for the Company's regulated property, plant and equipment are reviewed when the Company files a change in transmission rates with the FERC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company evaluates its property, plant and equipment for impairment when events or changes in circumstance indicate that the carrying value of such assets may not be recoverable. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On February 3, 2025, the Company filed an application with the FERC seeking to amend its existing Certificate of Public Convenience and Necessity to reflect the amended project for MVP Southgate. During the first quarter of 2025, the Company recognized expense of $40.8 million in account 426.5 in the Statement of Income related to the probable abandonment of certain construction work in progress assets associated with portions of the originally certificated MVP Southgate project that are no longer expected to provide future economic benefit. No indicators of impairment were identified during 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Allowance for Funds Used During Construction (AFUDC). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;AFUDC represents the capitalization of financing costs associated with constructing long-lived assets and includes both an equity component and an interest component. The FERC prescribes a formula to be used for computing AFUDC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;For the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, the AFUDC rate for equity funds was 5.53% and 6.86%, respectively, and the AFUDC rate for borrowed funds was 2.95% and 2.94%, respectively. AFUDC recognized on equity funds, which is recorded in other income, was approximately $4.9 million and $129.8 million for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively. AFUDC recognized on borrowed funds, which is recorded as a reduction of other interest charges, was approximately $2.6 million and $55.6 million for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Intangible Assets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On July 21, 2021, MVP A entered into a Verified Emission Reduction Purchase Agreement (the VER Agreement) with NextEra Energy Marketing, LLC (NEM), an affiliate of NextEra, pursuant to which MVP A acquired carbon credits for the purpose of offsetting greenhouse gas emissions associated with the operation of MVP Mainline. On September 26, 2025, MVP A and NEM terminated the VER Agreement and entered into a Carbon Credits Purchase and Sale Agreement (the Carbon Credits Agreement), which serves the same purpose as the VER Agreement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Carbon credits purchased under the Carbon Credits Agreement are held-for-use and recognized as intangible assets upon purchase. The Company recognizes a carbon credit utilization expense in operating and maintenance expense based on estimated throughput volumes, with a corresponding credit to other current liabilities. Upon formal retirement of the carbon credits, which occurs periodically, the related intangible assets are derecognized and the accrual is relieved.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;During the year ended December 31, 2025, the Company recorded $5.5 million of carbon credit purchases as intangible assets and recognized $4.2 million of carbon credit utilization expense in operating and maintenance expense in the Statement of Income.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Prior to MVP Mainline being placed into service, purchases of carbon credits were funded by capital contributions from members. Under the VER Agreement, during the year ended December 31, 2024, the Company recorded $1.1 million of carbon credit purchases as intangible assets and recognized $1.8 million of carbon credit utilization expense.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Income Taxes. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;See Note "Income Taxes."&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Natural Gas Imbalances. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Natural gas imbalances arise when actual deliveries of natural gas differ from scheduled quantities. The Company measures imbalances with shippers and interconnecting operators at current index prices. Imbalances with shippers are generally settled in-kind, subject to the terms of the Company's tariff. Certain imbalances with interconnecting operators may require cash settlement if the imbalance exceeds specified thresholds. Any gain or loss associated with cash settlements, including related gas purchases or sales, is deferred to a regulatory asset or liability in accordance with the Company's tariff.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Imbalances due from others are recorded in the Balance Sheets as miscellaneous current and accrued assets, and imbalances owed to others are recorded in the Balance Sheets as miscellaneous current and accrued liabilities. All imbalances are classified as current in the Balance Sheets as the Company expects them to settle within one year.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Regulatory Accounting. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company's interstate transmission operations are regulated by the FERC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Rate regulation establishes the rates the Company may charge for regulated services and provides for the recovery of costs plus an authorized return on invested capital. Regulatory accounting permits the deferral of certain costs and income as regulated assets and liabilities when it is probable that such amounts will be recovered from, or refunded to, customers through future rates. These deferred amounts are recognized in the Statements of Income in the period in which the underlying costs and income are reflected in the rates charged by the Company to shippers and operators. The Company expects to continue to be subject to rate regulation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Deferred amounts recorded as regulatory assets and liabilities relate primarily to deferred taxes, AFUDC and the transmission retainage tracker on MVP Mainline.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Contingencies. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;See Note "Commitments and Contingencies."&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Asset Retirement Obligations. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company is under no legal or contractual obligation to restore or dismantle MVP Mainline. In addition, the Company is responsible for the operation and maintenance of MVP Mainline and intends to continue such operation and maintenance so long as supply and demand for natural gas exists. As the Company expects supply and demand for natural gas to exist into the foreseeable future, the Company has not recorded asset retirement obligations for MVP Mainline.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Revenue Recognition. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company provides transmission services under firm and interruptible service contracts.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Firm service contracts generally require the customer to pay a firm reservation fee, which is a fixed, monthly charge to reserve an agreed upon amount of pipeline capacity regardless of whether the customer uses the capacity. Under its firm service contracts, the Company has a stand-ready obligation to provide the firm service over the life of the contract. The performance obligation for revenue from firm reservation fees is satisfied over time as the pipeline capacity is made available to the customer. As such, the Company recognizes firm reservation fee revenue evenly over the contract period using a time-elapsed output method to measure progress.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Volumetric-based fees, which are charges based on the volume of gas transported, can also be charged under firm service contracts for each firm contracted volume transported as well as for volumes transported in excess of the firm contracted volume so long as capacity exists.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Interruptible service contracts require the customer to pay volumetric-based fees and generally do not guarantee access to the pipeline.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The performance obligation for revenue from volumetric-based fees is generally satisfied upon the Company's monthly invoicing to the customer for volumes transported during the month. The amount invoiced generally corresponds directly to the value of the Company's performance to date as the customer obtains value as each volume is transported. The Company's transmission service contracts are invoiced at the end of each calendar month, with payment typically due within 10 days of the invoice date. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;For both firm reservation and volumetric-based fee revenues, the Company allocates the transaction price to each performance obligation based on the estimated relative standalone selling price. Any excess of consideration received over revenue recognized results in the deferral of those amounts until future periods based on a units-of-production or straight-line methodology as these methods align with the consumption of services provided to the customer. The units-of-production methodology requires the use of judgment to estimate future production volumes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Distribution Policy. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Under the MVP LLC Agreement, all available cash with respect to each series of the Company is distributable to its members. The respective Management Committee of each series determines available cash for distribution on a quarterly basis and may establish cash reserves and require additional capital contributions, as necessary. Available cash consists of cash and cash equivalents on hand at the end of each quarter, net of reserves (as defined in the MVP LLC Agreement) established to fund the Company's operations, comply with applicable law or satisfy obligations under debt or other agreements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ffffff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;----------------&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;C. Rate and Other Regulatory Matters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On October 23, 2015, the Company filed an application in Docket No. CP16-10 under Section 7(c) of the Natural Gas Act to construct and operate MVP Mainline. MVP Mainline was designed to provide up to 2,000,000 dekatherms (Dth) per day of firm transportation service from Wetzel County, West Virginia to Transcontinental Pipe Line Company, LLC&#8217;s Compressor Station 165 in Pittsylvania County, Virginia. MVP Mainline consists of 303 miles of 42" diameter pipeline and three compressor stations located in Wetzel, Braxton and Fayette Counties in West Virginia. FERC issued the Final Environmental Impact Statement on June 23, 2017, and the Company received its certificate on October 13, 2017. The Company commenced construction on February 5, 2018. On February 19, 2021, the Company filed an amendment under Docket No. CP21-57 that authorized the Company to change the crossing method for specific wetlands and waterbodies from the open-cut crossings to one of several trenchless methods; on April 8, 2022, the Company received its Order Amending Certificate. MVP Mainline began commercial operations on June 14, 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On November 6, 2018, the Company filed an application in Docket No. CP19-14 under Section 7(c) of the Natural Gas Act to construct and operate MVP Southgate. MVP Southgate was originally designed to provide up to 375,000 Dth per day of firm transportation service to a delivery point with PSNC near Graham, North Carolina. MVP Southgate originally proposed to consist of approximately 73 miles of pipe, one compressor station, associated valves, piping and appurtenant facilities commencing near Chatham, Virginia. FERC issued the Final Environmental Impact Statement on February 14, 2020, and the Company received its certificate on June 18, 2020. On December 19, 2023, the Company received a three-year extension of time, until June 18, 2026, to complete construction of MVP Southgate. In late December 2023, the Company entered into precedent agreements with PSNC and Duke Energy Carolinas, LLC. These precedent agreements contemplate an amended project (in lieu of the originally certificated project) for which the Amendment Application was filed with FERC on February 3, 2025 in Docket No. CP25-60. The amended project would extend approximately 31 miles from the terminus of MVP Mainline in Pittsylvania County, Virginia to planned new delivery points in Rockingham County, North Carolina using 30-inch diameter pipe. The amended project would include substantially fewer water crossings and would not require a new compressor station. The new precedent agreements collectively provide for 550,000 dekatherms per day of firm capacity commitments. On October 3, 2025, FERC issued the Environmental Assessment for the amended project, and on December 18, 2025, FERC issued an Order Amending Certificate approving the amended project. On March 23, 2026, the FERC approved the Company's request to proceed with the construction of the MVP Southgate facilities in Virginia. The targeted completion timing for MVP Southgate is June 2028. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On June 3, 2019, the Company submitted under Docket No. CP19-477 an application to install a new metering and regulating (M&amp;amp;R) station, associated piping and a tap site in Monroe County, West Virginia (collectively, the Interconnect Project) under FERC&#8217;s prior notice regulations. The new interconnect facilities allow the Company to deliver up to approximately 1.0 billion cubic feet per day to Columbia Gas Transmission, LLC&#8217;s (Columbia) KA System. FERC issued an Environmental Assessment Report on August 13, 2019, and the Company received its Order Authorizing Construction on April 16, 2020. The Interconnect Project began commercial operations on June 14, 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On October 23, 2025, the Company filed an application in Docket No. CP26-14 under Section 7(c) of the Natural Gas Act to construct and operate MVP Boost. MVP Boost is designed to provide up to 600,000 dekatherms per day of additional firm transportation service on MVP Mainline. MVP Boost would add compression at three existing compressor stations on MVP Mainline in West Virginia and construct a new compressor station in Montgomery County, Virginia. MVP Boost is targeted to be in service by mid-2028.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;D. Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;In the ordinary course of business, the Company has transactions with related parties.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company has entered into a 20-year transportation service agreement with each of its members or an affiliate of each member (excluding NextEra and Vega) to transport natural gas on MVP Mainline. Under these transportation service agreements, the Company has contracted firm transportation commitments totaling approximately &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;1.7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt; Bcf per day on MVP Mainline, subject to any future capacity releases.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company recognized revenues from MVP A members of $506.9&#160;million and $234.3 million for the years ended &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;December 31, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Pursuant to the COM Agreements, EQM Gathering serves as operator of the Company, with EQT's employees providing operational support and managing the Company's daily business operations. Costs incurred by EQM Gathering and its affiliates related to the development, construction, marketing and operation of the Company's assets are reimbursable by the Company. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The tables below summarize the Company's related party amounts. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:62.590%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:16.757%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.395%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:16.758%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="9" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Year Ended December 31,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000